{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ויחנטו.</b> They embalmed his body after they had thrown into it the bitter spices, in order to draw out the filth in his intestines, and in order that it not rot, they threw into it afterward sweet spices to produce a good fragrance. And analogous to it is the fig when it embalms its unripe fruit, which sweetens its fruits."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:32.647152789Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}